You fight the incentive to run away immediately, but it looks there is nothing to fear. It's clear that the natives feel the mix of adoration, fear and admiration about you. In their opinion you are true gods restoring their fire. And, in principle, you almost didn't lie to them. Well, maybe a little bit.
Doyle grew bolder and speaks to the chief about something, then turns to you and says.
